/-!
# Small full-extension triality completions

The algebraic F.4.3 extension and whole-overlap hypotheses give faithful
seven-path actions with native unequal valences. The full extension order
bound proves order equality, girth twelve, diameter six and actual smallness,
including q=4. The marked native images generate a normal subgroup of exactly
the native order. Its own graph has diameter six, and the native Cartan-fixed
apartment puts the sixth-power defect in its literal Borel. Half-turn
inversion and odd Cartan order kill that defect. Paired comparison then
identifies the full extension with both endpoint equations, giving faithful
extension recognition and native recognition under simplicity. Twisting the
pure-inner model marking extends every compatible native pair automorphism,
without an ambient source order bound. None of these conclusions is a field
of the algebraic source extension interface.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith F.4.3--7, F.4.13 and F.4.24.
-/
